{"results":[{"url":"https://www.wsj.com/world/europe/thailands-king-becomes-a-foreign-relations-challenge-for-germany-11603733852","final_url":"https://www.wsj.com/world/europe/thailands-king-becomes-a-foreign-relations-challenge-for-germany-11603733852","title":"Thailand’s King Becomes a Foreign Relations Challenge for Germany","description":"Demonstrators marched to the German Embassy in Bangkok late Monday to ask Angela Merkel’s government to investigate their king, who spends stretches of time in Bavaria. ","language":"en","text":"Advertisement\n\n# Thailand’s King Becomes a Foreign Relations Challenge for Germany\n\n## Protesters in Bangkok ask Berlin to investigate their monarch’s stays in Bavaria\n\nBy\n\nFeliz Solomon\n\nin Singapore and\n\nRuth Bender\n\nin Berlin\n\nMass protests in Thailand have shaken the nation with criticism of the country’s powerful and secretive royal family. WSJ’s Feliz Solomon explains what the protesters are fighting for and why their demands could land them in jail. Photo: Lillian Suwanrumpha/AFP/Getty Images\n\nPro-democracy protesters in Thailand who are taking on their country’s powerful and secretive monarchy are turning to Germany for answers.\n\nThousands of demonstrators marched to the gates of the German Embassy in Bangkok late Monday to ask Angela Merkel’s government to investigate their king, who spends stretches of time in the southern German state of Bavaria.\n\nCopyright ©2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. 87990cbe856818d5eddac44c7b1cdeb8\n\n## Videos","author":"Feliz Solomon in Singapore and Ruth Bender in Berlin","published_date":"2020-10-26T17:37:00Z","latency_ms":13140.571308991639,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}